  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;GREG BOYER (MUSICIAN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greg Boyer (musician) is an American trombonist known for performing with many successful R&amp;B and funk bands. He was born in Washington, DC, and grew up in Bryans Road, Maryland. He excelled in playing various instruments and was primarily focused on classical tuba."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASHINGTON, DC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Washington, DC is the birthplace of Greg Boyer (musician&lt;SEP&gt;"Washington, DC is the birthplace of Greg Boyer (musician)."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRYANS ROAD, MARYLAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bryans Road, Maryland is where Greg Boyer (musician&lt;SEP&gt;"Bryans Road, Maryland is where Greg Boyer (musician) grew up."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACKEY HIGH SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lackey High School is the school Greg Boyer (musician&lt;SEP&gt;"Lackey High School is the school Greg Boyer (musician) graduated from, where he became proficient in playing various instruments."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREG BOYER (CHEF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greg Boyer (chef&lt;SEP&gt;"Greg Boyer (chef) is an American chef known for his innovative culinary techniques and blending traditional and modern flavors. He was born in Washington, DC, and grew up in Bryans Road, Maryland. He started cooking at an early age and by the time he graduated from Lackey High School, he could prepare a wide variety of dishes."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREGORY VAITL 'GREG' BOYER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gregory Vaitl 'Greg' Boyer is a former American water polo player who won a silver medal at the 1988 Summer Olympics in Seoul, South Korea. He grew up in New York City and played water polo at Aviation High School. He attended the University of California, Santa Barbara where he played on the Gauchos men's water polo team from 1976-1979."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW YORK CITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New York City is the place where Gregory Vaitl 'Greg' Boyer grew up."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AVIATION HIGH SCHOOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aviation High School is the school where Gregory Vaitl 'Greg' Boyer played water polo."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNIVERSITY OF CALIFORNIA, SANTA BARBARA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"University of California, Santa Barbara is the university where Gregory Vaitl 'Greg' Boyer played water polo and was named a three-time All-American."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0209-0f350c9aa919</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES MEN'S NATIONAL WATER POLO TEAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The United States men's national water polo team is the team Gregory Vaitl 'Greg' Boyer was a member of and won a silver medal at the 1988 Summer Olympics."(</data>
